======================================================================
INTERPRETATION
======================================================================
  • If the α-helix region is BLUE (negative Δτ): τ is compressed
    there — consistent with the helix H-bond pulling N-Cα and
    Cα-C closer together.
  • If the β-sheet region is RED (positive Δτ): τ is expanded
    there — consistent with extended-chain geometry relaxing
    the sp³ constraint.
  • Signal/noise > 1 means the effect is real, not shot noise.
  • If the map is flat: either there's no mechanical effect,
    OR it's swamped by residue-composition drift — stratify
    by residue type (Option 1) as a sanity check.
